# Archives — may be created during development uploads; never commit
*.[zZ][iI][pP]

# Personal financial data — must never be committed to source control.
# Reference payslips live OUTSIDE this repo at ../roster-private/payslips/
# so they can never be accidentally committed. These rules are a safety net
# in case any payslip/screenshot is ever dropped into the working tree.
# EITHER CASE: matching is case-sensitive on Linux, where sessions run, and a phone or a scanner
# names its files IMG_0042.JPG, IMG_0042.HEIC and SCAN.PDF. (The Links 26 PDFs are force-added.)
*.[pP][dD][fF]
*.[jJ][pP][gG]
*.[jJ][pP][eE][gG]
*.[hH][eE][iI][cC]
example-payslips/

# THE FILES THE DOCUMENTED WORKFLOWS ACTUALLY BRING IN (whole-app check, 10 November 2026). The depot
# annual-leave workbook names every colleague against their leave (docs/AL_WORKBOOK.md), and its own
# recipe unzips `xl/` out of it in the working directory; a Huddle is a Word document. None of these
# kinds is tracked anywhere, and the Pages mirror would serve whatever one `git add -A` committed.
*.[xX][lL][sS][xX]
*.[xX][lL][sS]
*.[cC][sS][vV]
*.[dD][oO][cC][xX]
xl/

# Node dependencies
node_modules/
functions/node_modules/

# Playwright test output (reports and traces — local inspection only, not committed)
playwright-report/
test-results/

# Claude Code agent worktrees — temporary working directories, never commit
.claude/worktrees/

# Local env / secrets
.env
.env.*
firestore-debug.log
firebase-debug.log
ui-debug.log

# REAL PAYSLIP FIGURES NEVER ENTER THE TREE (v23.71).
# `test-fixtures/payslip-actuals.local.js` holds a member's actual payslips — the regression net
# behind the pay maths. It is excluded from Firebase Hosting, but the GitHub Pages mirror serves the
# repository root with no ignore list, so anything committed here is published there. A gitignore is
# the only rule both origins obey. `test-fixtures/payslip-actuals.example.js` documents the shape.
*.local.js

# The AL workbook reconciliation log — names colleagues against their leave figures, and
# `docs/` is served by the GitHub Pages mirror at HTTP 200. Same rule as the payslip fixture, and
# the same glob: doc-parity.test.mjs exempts EVERY `*.local.md` from its index as gitignored, so a
# second private log named by the convention must be ignored too, not only this one path.
*.local.md
